    },
    {
      "text": "Lay salmon on a platter and pour half of the marinade on top. Turn the pieces to make sure the marinade is on all sides. Cover and chill for 1 hour.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/asian-style-salmon-with-portobello-and-baby-bok-choy/#wprm-recipe-59548-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/asian-style-salmon-with-portobello-and-baby-bok-choy-step-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 400F. Trim the vegetables. Halve the bok choy and cut the mushrooms into 1/2 inch slices. Coat with the remaining marinade.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/asian-style-salmon-with-portobello-and-baby-bok-choy/#wprm-recipe-59548-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/asian-style-salmon-with-portobello-and-baby-bok-choy-step-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the marinated vegetables and salmon on a lined baking sheet. The salmon should be skin side down.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/asian-style-salmon-with-portobello-and-baby-bok-choy/#wprm-recipe-59548-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/asian-style-salmon-with-portobello-and-baby-bok-choy-step-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the oven for 20 minutes, or until the salmon is cooked through. Once done, it should flake easily. Garnish with sliced green onions and sesame seeds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/asian-style-salmon-with-portobello-and-baby-bok-choy/#wprm-recipe-59548-step-0-4",
